Issue: 
 After upgrading to Crystal Reports 13.0.26.3348 runtime, ReportDocument.Export() is failing with 'Failed to Open Connection', even though same DB access credentials work in rest of the application and also worked with previous Crystal Report Runtime versions with same code. 

 Error: 
 System.Runtime.InteropServices.COMException (0x800002F4): Failed to open the connection. SampleReport.rpt 
 at Crystal Decisions. ReportAppServer.Controllers: DatabaseControllerClass.SetTableLocation (ISCRTable CurTable, ISCRTable NewTable) 
 at CrystalDecisions.Crystal Reports.Engine.Table.set_Location (String value) 
 at Ecstra. ReportGenerator.ReportGenerator.SetConnectionInfo (ConnectionInfo connectionInfo, Table table) 
 at Ecstra. ReportGenerator. ReportGenerator. Export Report (Report Info report Info, ReportDocument doc) 
 System.Runtime.InteropServices.COMException (0x8004100F): Error in File SampleReport.гpt: 
 Unable to connect incorrect log on parameters. 
 Details: [Database Vendor Code: 30156] 
 at Crystal Decisions. ReportAppServer.Controllers.DatabaseControllerClass.SetTableLocation (ISCRTable CurTable, ISCRTable NewTable) 
 at Crystal Decisions. Crystal Reports.Engine.Table.set Location (String value) 
 at Ecstra. ReportGenerator. ReportGenerator.SetConnectionInfo (ConnectionInfo connectionInfo, Table table) 
 at Ecstra. ReportGenerator.ReportGenerator.ExportReport (ReportInfo reportInfo, Report Document doc) 

 Code: 
 void ExportReport (ReportInfo report Info, Report Document doc) 
 { 
 var kerberos ConnectionInfo = new Crystal Decisions.Shared.ConnectionInfo(); 
 kerberosConnectionInfo.ServerName = connectionInfo.ServerName; // DSN 
 kerberosConnectionInfo.DatabaseName = connectionInfo.DatabaseName; 
 kerberosConnectionInfo.IntegratedSecurity = true; 
 kerberosConnectionInfo.UserID = ""; 
 kerberosConnectionInfo.Password = ""; 
 ApplyConnectionInfoSafely (doc, kerberosConnectionInfo, false); 
 doc.VerifyDatabase(); //FAILS connection validation at export time rejects it. If we don't add this line, it fails in next line in 'Export' 

 doc.Export(); 
 } 
 void ApplyConnectionInfoToTable (Table table, Connection Info connectionInfo, ...) 
 { 
 var logonInfo= table.LogOnInfo; 
 logonInfo.ConnectionInfo.ServerName = connectionInfo.ServerName; 
 logonInfo.ConnectionInfo.DatabaseName = connectionInfo.DatabaseName; 
 logonInfo.ConnectionInfo.IntegratedSecurity = connectionInfo. IntegratedSecurity; 
 logonInfo.ConnectionInfo.UserID = connectionInfo.UserID; 
 logonInfo.ConnectionInfo.Password = connectionInfo.Password; 
 table.ApplyLogon Info (logonInfo); //SUCCEEDS connection info is accepted and stored 
 } 

 Environment details: 
 Crystal Reports Version - 13,0.25.3158 (SAP Crystal Reports 2020) 
 Target Database - Sybase (SQL) 
 Authentication Method - Kerberos (MIT Kerberos) 
 DSN Configuration - DSN created with Kerberos on client machine 
 Framework - .NET with Crystal Report assemblies
